  "narrative": {
    "intro": "BL Harbert International has $971M in federal contract obligations for FY2026 to date across 47 awards, with an average award size of $20.6M and obligations up 3.4% year over year. BL Harbert International has recorded multi-year activity: FY21 obligations were $488M, FY22 obligations were $1.7B, FY23 obligations were $1.3B, FY24 obligations were $1B, and FY25 obligations were $938M. BL Harbert International derives the large majority of FY2026 to date obligations from one buyer. The Department of Defense obligated $925M to BL Harbert International in FY2026 to date. BL Harbert International receives smaller amounts from other agencies: the Department of State obligated $35.6M, the Department of Justice obligated $9.5M, the National Aeronautics and Space Administration obligated $225K, the General Services Administration obligated $220K, and the Department of Homeland Security obligated $10K. BL Harbert International’s work in FY2026 to date is concentrated in construction markets. Commercial and Institutional Building Construction accounts for $921M of obligations, followed by Power and Communication Line and Related Structures Construction with $45.2M, Architectural Services with $4.3M, and Industrial Building Construction with $50K.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "How concentrated are BL Harbert International’s federal obligations?",
        "body": "BL Harbert International shows high concentration with the Department of Defense at $925M in FY2026 to date. BL Harbert International has $921M in Commercial and Institutional Building Construction obligations, indicating sector concentration. BL Harbert International records much smaller obligations across other agencies and NAICS, which makes the portfolio dependent on a few large awards."
      },
      {
        "heading": "How has BL Harbert International’s federal business changed over recent fiscal years?",
        "body": "BL Harbert International had $488M in FY21 and then rose to $1.7B in FY22. BL Harbert International obligations moved to $1.3B in FY23, $1B in FY24, $938M in FY25, and $971M in FY26 to date. BL Harbert International shows a year-over-year change of up 3.4% for the current fiscal year to date."
      }
    ]
